  "why": "No event after 26 January 2024 touches the converse: every one is about the forward theorem, an analogue (Gaussian, quadratic, q-, Lucas-type), a different congruence, or (Pimenova) unread, so they are variant or none. The pre-snapshot results are partial: Trevisan-Weber (even n), Helou-Terjanian (families) and Hussein's Proposition 4 (n = m·p^k family) are cases; McIntosh's check to 10⁹ is instances; Broughan-Luca-Shparlinski's density bound on the mod-n set is read as a bound on the mod-n³ composite set. None is whole, so nothing pre-snapshot is resolved. The Guedes-Machado restatement is dated to its 2023 journal version but scores none either way. Linhares formalises and re-proves the known forward theorem, which is a different question. Its AI credits (Deep Vision finding the proof, Claude writing Lean proofs) are about formalising a known result, not mathematics in a result on this problem, so ai_role is none.",
